{"user": "quick follow up now that its done - why did playing h1 before g2 matter so much? I assumed order was safe either way but you said it wasn't", "user_ts": "2026-08-12T20:12:28.433338+00:00", "assistant": "Because **g2 is the X-square next to the h1 corner**.\n\nIf you play **g2 before h1**, you create this White legal move:\n\n**h1 \u2192 g2 (black) \u2192 f3 (white)**\n\nSo White can suddenly play **h1**, take the corner, and likely flip **g2** back. Corners are permanent, so that\u2019s a huge swing.\n\nBy playing **h1 first**, you lock the corner for Black. Then White still has no move, and **g2 becomes safe as the final cleanup square**.\n\nSo the key rule: **don\u2019t fill the X-square before you own the adjacent corner**, unless you\u2019ve counted that it can\u2019t be used.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-12T20:12:28.433338+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-12T20:12:33.433338+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Metacomment"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Metacomment"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 1, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 3, "Metacomment": 2}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 0.3333333333333333, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0, "Metacomment": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"llama": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Metacomment"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Metacomment"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Local Justification", "Worked Line", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Local Justification", "Worked Line", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Local Justification": 3, "Worked Line": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Move Verdict": 1}, "confidence": {"Local Justification": 1.0, "Worked Line": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0, "Move Verdict": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Local Justification", "Worked Line", "General